content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal drip of approximately 1 drop/second: no numerical allowable seal-leakage limit is provided, so a numerical pass/fail comparison cannot be made. The applicable manual troubleshooting entry is 'Leakage at shaft seal', which requires mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.4 mm/s: the applicable documented limits are Figure 3's HF-300 vibration zones, expressed as mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. Numerically, 3.4 is in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), 'Long-term operation': above the 2.8 Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 Zone B/C boundary. It is not in Zone C, 'Restricted - plan maintenance', or Zone D (7.1–11.0), 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The SSP-07 immediate-stop control for the highest severity zone is therefore not triggered by this reading, subject to confirming the measurement basis.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature of 70 C: applying the manual's bearing-housing temperature limits, normal operation is up to 70 C, alarm is 80 C and trip is 90 C. The reading is exactly at the upper normal limit, 10 C below alarm and 20 C below trip. It does not trigger SSP-07's requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift, which applies only when bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Operational disposition: the supplied vibration and temperature readings do not require an immediate stop, but the active shaft-seal leakage requires corrective maintenance. P2 is assigned for planned seal replacement and investigation rather than emergency work.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Early seal failure or worn/cracked seal faces is most likely because shaft-seal leakage directly matches those manual causes. If the installed seal is HF3-450, applicability is strengthened by SB-2026-014, which documents early HF3-450 failures caused by a revised sleeve tolerance on pumps built from serial HF3-22000; P-104 is serial HF3-22871.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a common documented cause of both shaft-seal leakage and high vibration, so it is the next checksToPerformPriorityCandidate.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry, another documented cause of shaft-seal leakage. The HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; flush/dry-running history needs verification.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation remain possible contributors to the vibration reading. The manual directs inspection of bearings and impeller and an NPSH check for the vibration symptom.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Before internal or seal work, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent the line, and obtain the line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly. Its mass is 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg lifting-control threshold; use the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment specified in the safety controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and record the scoring depth and removed seal type. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the accompanying symptoms: check shaft alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller, and check NPSH. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair rather than replacing only one.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. No sleeve measurement is needed to set HF3-450B. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the fasteners. For the applicable Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm where disturbed. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014; the manual's 25 Nm gland torque does not apply to this installation.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out the required alignment check with a laser alignment tool, and repeat laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Documented tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, verify the seal-flush arrangement is Plan 11 from pump discharge and ensure the pump is not run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on this in-scope serial number. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new whenever the casing is opened and during mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional replacement part, required if inspection finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. P-104 is within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For removal of the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment, because the component exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional vibration hold: if vibration is subsequently measured in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS on bearing housings), stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The current 3.4 mm/s reading is numerically in Zone B and does not activate this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard labour time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour time 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement: if inspection requires replacement of the bearing pair, the standard labour time is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians; this is not part of the base seal-replacement labour unless triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection and gland torque conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies specifically to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and requires HF3-450B with a 30 Nm gland torque; pumps below HF3-22000 continue with HF3-450 and Table 5. P-104 is HF3-22871 and is therefore within the bulletin's serial range, so the bulletin governs: do not fit HF3-450 and do not use 25 Nm for the HF3-450B gland. The previous-shift instruction to ignore the bulletin and use 25 Nm for all pumps is not valid for this asset. The other Table 5 torques remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does the reported 3.4 mm/s vibration value represent RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, as required by Figure 3? The report does not state the RMS or measurement-location basis, so confirm this before treating Zone B as the final classification (C07).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and is there any history of seal-flush loss or dry running? This is needed to confirm whether the bulletin's documented HF3-450 early-failure mechanism or run-dry damage applies (C02, C09, C13).",
    "What are the sleeve scoring depth, alignment readings, bearing and impeller inspection results, and NPSH check results? These determine whether the conditional sleeve, paired-bearing work, or other additional corrective work is required (C05, C09, C10, C13).",
    "What numerical seal-leakage acceptance criterion, if any, applies after repair? The evidence identifies leakage and its corrective action but provides no allowable drip rate (C09).",
    "What response-time target applies to P2 at this site? The evidence documents only the priority-1 trigger for bearing temperature above alarm; P2 is assigned here because seal work is required but neither that P1 trigger nor the immediate-stop vibration trigger is met (C02, C07, C09, C15)."
  ]
}
